{
  "id": "80619",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Relative Rates of Reaction",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "So far, we have dealt with reaction rates only for reactions with 1:1 stoichiometry. We next consider how to determine reaction rates for reactions with other stoichiometric ratios, such as the decomposition of ammonia:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "ec5d2xtxex476yr",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "vdvhxw2klrb8o51",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "5c14b70lod0erz3",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm{NH}}_3(g)\\;\\longrightarrow\\;{\\mathrm N}_2(g)\\;+\\;3\\;{\\mathrm H}_2(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "We can follow this reaction in terms of the rate of disappearance of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the rate of appearance of N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", or the rate of appearance of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ". When this reaction occurs, 3 mol H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " form and 2 mol NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " decompose for every 1 mol N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " that forms. Therefore, the rate of increase in the concentration of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " is three times the rate of increase in the concentration of N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " (or alternatively, the rate at which [N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] increases is one-third the rate at which [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] increases):"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vilgpjavju5zsln",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "07mnanpgm1z0reo",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "udmmnw4u7g6qu5o",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_2\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\;=\\;3\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm N}_2\\rbrack} {\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm N}_2\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\; =\\;\\frac13\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_2\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Similarly, the rate of decrease in the concentration of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " is two times the rate of increase in the concentration of N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " (or the rate at which [NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "] decreases is one-half the rate at which [N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] increases):"
              }
            ],
            "id": "jinbczw5npg50yi",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "n5iyy1xhdbxbxp7",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2a0x41ypuh3gwpv",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "-\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm{NH}}_3\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\;=\\;2\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm N}_2\\rbrack} {\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm N}_2\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\; =\\;-\\frac12\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack{\\mathrm{NH}}_3\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Note that a negative sign has been added to account for the decreasing concentration of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "dgmb7gtpq22flsx",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The graphs in the following slides show the concentration changes over time when ammonia decomposes into nitrogen and hydrogen at 1100 °C. We can see that for a given time interval, the concentration changes of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": ", N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " are related by their stoichiometric factors."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p6siz8dowxnr2lw",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "zxkvp8d8qm0sy51",
                "text": "Slide Show"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0vzh5klq0p5mqcw",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Click "
              },
              {
                "strong": true,
