        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The rate of a reaction may be expressed in terms of the change in the amount of any reactant or product. Different substances in a reaction may have different rates of change, but for any given reaction, these rate expressions are all related to one another according to the reaction stoichiometry. From the relationships between these relative rates, we define a rate of reaction that does not depend on which reactant or product is used."
              }
            ],
            "id": "mxlkgpqy8zwtjeu",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "s4qgxfs1rnyvlum",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "jts28vppqbcurhw",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "oqpedpsnevwk0zq",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "nlwrp2jzd199h7c",
            "items": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1348602384",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "For the following general reaction, the reaction rate can be expressed in terms of the decrease in the concentration of A or B or the increase in the concentration of C or D:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "a\\mathrm A\\;+\\;b\\mathrm B\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;c\\mathrm C\\;+\\;d\\mathrm D",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "These four rate expressions are related by the stoichiometry of the reaction, and we define the rate of reaction as:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "\\mathrm{Reaction}\\;\\mathrm{rate}\\;=\\;-\\frac1a\\frac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}{\\Delta t}\\;=\\;-\\frac1b\\frac {\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}{\\Delta t}\\;=\\;\\frac1c\\frac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm C\\right]}{\\Delta t}\\; =\\;\\frac1d\\frac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm D\\right]}{\\Delta t}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "This definition means the rate of reaction will be the same no matter which substance we use to track the concentration changes for the reaction. It allows us to talk about the rate of the reaction without specifying a particular reactant or product."
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3783057270",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "dd"
              }
            ],
            "title": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " Relative Rates of Reaction "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3559840167",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "type": "dl"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ncv7g618bz0n4ge",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "hgh12vtv7popu3i",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "2809353776",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1205977804",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
